# What the source distribution carries beyond the package itself.
#
# Without this file setuptools falls back to its legacy sdist finder: the package plus files
# matching the literal glob tests/test*.py. That silently dropped tests/support.py (imported by
# 18 of 21 test modules), tests/__init__.py, and all of tools/ - so anyone who did what a
# distro packager or a reproducibility auditor does, `pip download --no-binary :all:` then
# `python -m unittest discover -s tests`, got 18 ModuleNotFoundErrors from a project whose
# README says "clone and run, zero build step". Found by the pre-release adversarial pass
# against the live 0.7.0 sdist; the wheel was never affected. tools/assert_dist_roundtrip.py
# now extracts the built sdist and runs its suite, so this cannot regress unnoticed.
include README.md CHANGELOG.md CORRECTIONS.md PREREGISTRATION.md PROVENANCE.md CONTRIBUTING.md SECURITY.md LICENSE
recursive-include tests *.py
recursive-include tools *.py
recursive-include evidence *.json
